<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 90,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Monday 90,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts Monday were estimated at 90,000 head, compared with 97,000 a week ago and 77,000 a year ago, USDA said.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were firm to $0.50 per cwt higher than midsession Friday.</p>
<p>Trade and demand was light to moderate with a few plants not slaughtering due to plant holiday. Offerings moderate.</p>
